  "text": "CasePath\nEvidence into action\nNew claim ↗\nCases\nDemonstration\nKnowledge\n\nCases / Recorded investigation\n\nRepeated heating failure and reported repair calls\n\nHistorical synthetic recording · as of 2025-02-21 · rules-based · No external action\n\nChoose case\nHistory\nFrom the sources\n02-heating-service-observation.txt\n↗\nOn 2025-02-21 at07:30, a calibrated digital instrument (calibration check2024-12-15, uncertainty±0.2C) measured the living room at15.8C after overnight normal operation. Main living rooms stayed15.5–16.3C in the seven-day logger record. Resets restore heat briefly; the pump cuts out repeatedly. The fixed circulation pump has an internal bearing/control failure; it is part of landlord-maintained equipment, outside ordinary small tenant maintenance. Normal ventilation and unobstructed radiators were observed; no tenant alteration or misuse explains the failure.\nWhat this shows\n\nThe dated calibrated observation identifies the fixed-pump fault and its causal limits.\n\nEstablished\n\nAssess objective defect evidence\nOpen larger process\n✓\nCapture the reported defect\n✓\nEstablish relevant tenancy terms\n✓\nEstablish landlord knowledge\n✓\nAssess supported cause\n✓\nAssess objective defect evidence\nCompleted\n✓\nRecord repair and rent reduction eligibility\nDocument requirements\nRelevant tenancy terms\nEstablished\nSupplied evidence is sufficient. ✓\nEstablish relevant tenancy terms\nSource evidence · 01-customer-and-tenancy-clarification.txt\nLandlord knowledge and continuing repair status\nEstablished\nSupplied evidence is sufficient. ✓\nEstablish landlord knowledge\nSource evidence · 03-landlord-knowledge-and-repair-status.txt\nDated technical defect observation\nEstablished\nSupplied evidence is sufficient. ✓\nAssess objective defect evidence\nSource evidence · 02-heating-service-observation.txt\nAll recorded requirements",
